# q2p1_viscometer - default particle file = V0 baseline (phi = 0).
#
# Lines that do not parse as three floats are ignored by
# readVectorsFromFile (libs/pe/pe/interface/geometry_utils.h:38-47),
# so these comments are safe.
#
# The PE serial setup used by this application (setupDraftKissTumbSerial,
# libs/pe/pe/interface/sim_setup_serial.h:1461-1469) THROWS a
# std::runtime_error when the xyz file yields zero positions, and an
# absent file yields the same (readVectorsFromFile returns empty on open
# failure).  A truly empty V0 is therefore not possible without patching
# the PE setup.
#
# Instead V0 uses exactly one "parked" sphere at the centre of the
# un-meshed bob bore.  The bore (r < 4, 4 <= z <= 12) contains no fluid
# DOFs at all; the nearest fluid DOFs sit on the bore surface at r = 4,
# i.e. 4 d away from a sphere of radius 0.5.  No DOF is ever covered, so
# FictKNPR stays 0 everywhere and the fluid solution is identical to a
# particle-free run.  With gravity_ = [0,0,0] the sphere never moves.
#
# For V1 (phi = 0.05) replace the single line below by the RSA packing of
# ~200 sphere centres in the annulus (margins: 0.5 d to walls, 1 d to the
# bob bottom and the lid).
0.0 0.0 8.0
